At stage n+1, a function clause yields stage-n consistency of the output union of a subcollection whenever the input union is stage-n consistent and contains no function tokens. Nested function tokens in a general input union are left to the general consistency argument.

If the subcollection is empty, the output union is empty and hence consistent at stage n. Otherwise the original finset contains a function token, so some earlier function clause exists, and the atom-input lift applies that clause at stage n.
